// REJECTS: 'DataQuality' is not a known section parser
//
// ENVIRONMENTAL-LOOKING, AND DELIBERATELY SO. The same message a missing extension gives.
// ../fixtures/t2-dataquality.pure parses using `###DataQualityValidation`, which proves the
// extension is loaded and the rejection here is about the NAME.
//
// The section is `###DataQualityValidation`, not `###DataQuality` -- the name registered by
// DataQualityGrammarParserExtension is the ELEMENT's name, not the vendor's. Every other
// grammar in this batch splits the two differently and none of the splits is guessable:
// BigQueryFunction registers `###BigQuery`, MemSqlFunction registers `###MemSql`,
// SnowflakeApp registers `###Snowflake`. Three shortenings and one that does not shorten.
//
// Pinned because a wrong section name is the one error whose message a rewrite is most
// likely to get right for the wrong reason: "not a known section parser" is also what a
// MISSING EXTENSION produces. ../fixtures/t2-dataquality.pure parses against the same
// classpath, so the DataQuality extension is present and this rejection is about the name.
//
// The body below is valid DataQualityValidation -- it is the second element of that fixture
// verbatim -- so nothing but the section header can be responsible.
###DataQuality
DataQualityValidation fixture::neg::WrongSectionName
{
   context: fromMappingAndRuntime(fixture::neg::M, fixture::neg::R);
   validationTree: $[ fixture::neg::Person { name } ]$;
}
